cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the archived measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "StreamViz: an instrumented testbed for latency-freshness trade-offs in streaming visualisation"
abstract: >-
  StreamViz measures what a real-time display does when the producer outruns the
  renderer. The display buffer's admission policy is an experimental variable
  (drop-oldest, drop-newest, block, unbounded); discards are attributed at each
  pipeline stage under a four-stage conservation contract; and staleness is
  defined as the age of the newest sample in a frame at the moment the frame
  becomes visible. The repository ships the measurement harness, two domain
  adapters over published recordings, a one-function adapter template, a
  downstream analysis consumer that shows what a second subscriber inherits
  from the policy, an audit tool that re-derives every published conservation
  identity from the archived JSON, and the archived outputs behind every
  reported number.
type: software
